      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Sales was fast to respond and provided all the information I needed.Installation went OK but there were a few things that I led me to minus a star:- They asked me to give my WIFI password so they can setup the Fronius inverter. That's not something anyone should have to give that info out to a complete stranger.- Panels were covered all over in brown dust, and still are, from Day 1.- Inverter cover was also covered in brown dust, and still is.Customer service is absolutely the worst. They started organising an inspector 13 days after. It didn't stop them from sending the bill for the balance. I tried to find out when an inspector will come but didn't get a response. 7 days later for inspector to do his check, which took 10mins tops. That's 13 days of not being able to use the solar panels.I had to call my energy supplier and utilities company to get things moving. After a few phone calls to Watters, I managed to get them to submit the paperwork to the energy supplier, but they stuffed that up by sending the wrong inverter serial number. More phone calls and emails later and that got sorted eventually.It's now been a month and I'm still not connected to the grid. The utilities company says it will take 15 days to reprogram the smart meter.Would I recommend them to others? No.",
